K5 PASS max|rho_ij| = 0.36, cond = 622 <0.5 and cond<1e4 :: the eight-bin jackknife covariance is close to diagonal, so a diagonal fit is not misleading; the full covariance with eigenvalues clipped at 1e-2 of the largest is used throughout, and the diagonal is reported as a cross-check

============================================================================================================
K6-K7  the algebra of u and A (exact, sympy), and the model reimplementation (bit-exact)
============================================================================================================
K6 PASS 0e+00 / 0e+00 / 0e+00 <1e-25 :: u = (P_l-P_N)/(D-P_N) is exactly D = P_N + (P_l-P_N)/u, and A = D/P_l = f_b + (1/u)(1-f_b) with f_b = P_N/P_l; dln(kA)/dlnR = dlnA/dlnR, so the log-slope diagnostic is invariant under any rescaling of the amplitude -- a shape match cannot be bought by rescaling
K7 PASS max rel dev = 2.2e-15 (4 clusters x 8 bins) <1e-10 :: the reimplementation of CFG687's `law()` (cored beta-profile baryons, nu_mono, exact spherical projection) reproduces the stored PL and PN arrays to machine precision, so the u(r) machinery below is the same model the record fitted

