K8 PASS u_in = 0.4371+-0.0288, chi2 = 9.96/7 = 1.42, max|resid| = 2.15sigma chi2/dof<2, 0.30<u_in<0.60, max resid<3.5sigma :: ONE free parameter (u_in) fits the full eight-bin profile at chi2/dof = 1.42: u_in = 0.437 +- 0.029, u = 1 fixed outside r_sp. No amplitude, shape or normalisation freedom is used -- the phantom's shape and the cosmic-share normalisation are CFG687's/A18's own
K9 PASS per-cluster r_sp: u_in = 0.4057+-0.0279, chi2/dof = 1.19; fixed-vs-cluster 0.78sigma chi2/dof<2 and the two variants agree <1.5sigma :: the theory's actual prediction is a step at each cluster's OWN r_sp ~ M^(1/3) (spread 16-84 pct = 0.94-1.90 Mpc), which broadens the stacked transition with zero extra parameters; it fits at chi2/dof = 1.19 and agrees with the fixed-r_sp fit to 0.78 sigma
  cosmic-share routes: A18 anchor R_tot = 2.618 -> u_CS = 0.488; stack self-consistent R_tot = 2.894 -> 0.540; CFG687 baryon budget R_tot = 2.765 -> 0.515
K10 PASS u_in = 0.437+-0.029; cosmic share u_CS = 0.514 (routes 0.488/0.540/0.515); Z = -1.3 |Z| < 3 vs the cosmic-share normalisation :: the cosmic-share normalisation M_c = 5.3643 M_b, recomputed for THIS stack (R_tot = 2.894 at M200c = 1.49e+14, c = 4.5) rather than copied from A18, predicts u = R_tot/5.3643 = 0.540; A18's anchor gives 0.488. The fit sits -1.3 sigma away from the three-route central value 0.514 +- 0.05, at the low end of the normalisation's own spread

