K11 PASS u=1: chi2 = 82.9/8 = 10.4; dchi2 = 73 (8.5 sigma) dchi2 > 49 (7 sigma) :: RIVAL (a) 'cold = exactly the law's phantom, u=1 everywhere' is excluded by the full profile at Delta chi2 = 73 (8.5 sigma), the same verdict as A18's 7.7 sigma band-ratio test and slightly stronger because all eight bins are used
K12 PASS u=0.4716: chi2 = 49.0/8; dchi2 = 39 (6.3 sigma) dchi2 > 16 (4 sigma) :: RIVAL (b) 'u = 0.472 everywhere' (A21's MID value, the best single number) is excluded: it fits the inner six bins but over-predicts the two outer ones by 6.9 and 8.7 sigma. The constant needs u = 0.566 to compromise, and that is still rejected at 5.5 sigma
K13 PASS u=0.488: chi2 = 45.7/8; dchi2 = 36 (6.0 sigma) dchi2 > 16 :: RIVAL (c) 'the cosmic share with the law's phantom shape, u = 0.488 everywhere' (A18's zero-parameter reading) is excluded as a CONSTANT: the cosmic share may set the total cold budget, but it cannot be applied uniformly in radius
K14 PASS best constant u = 0.566; chi2 = 39.9/8; dchi2 = 30 (5.5 sigma) dchi2 > 20 :: even the BEST constant u (fitted, u = 0.566) is rejected against the one-parameter step at Delta chi2 = 30 with the same number of parameters: the failure is not the value of u, it is that u is not constant in radius
K15 PASS step 1.42/dof vs const 4.99/dof vs u=1 10.4/dof; u_in vs A21 MID = 0.75 sigma ordered chi2, u_in consistent with A21's MID :: the ordering is step << best-constant < u=0.472 < u=1, and the fitted u_in = 0.437 agrees with A21's MID value 0.4716 +- 0.0362 (0.7 sigma): the full profile does not move the inner amplitude, it fixes the outer one

