============================================================================================================
K19-K21  what the step can and cannot be: the 3D realisation, the NFW rival, the width
============================================================================================================

  3D check: u=1 reproduces PL to 6.7e-16; 3D step best fit u_in = 0.557, chi2 = 37.1/7 = 5.3
  3D model A(R) = 1.60 1.60 1.62 1.64 1.67 1.74 1.71 1.47
  measured A(R) = 2.80 2.27 2.53 2.09 2.15 1.73 0.93 1.06
  3D resid/sd    = +1.1 +1.1 +2.7 +1.5 +2.3 -0.1 -5.3 -3.9
  the 3D step needs 1.2e+14 Msun of extra
  cold mass inside r_sp (cluster 0), i.e. 0.82 M200c
K19 PASS 3D step chi2 = 37.1/7 vs projected step 10.0/7; dchi2 = 27 (5.2 sigma); A(1.71) = 1.71 vs 0.93 measured dchi2 > 15 :: the step CANNOT be realised as a spherical amplification of the phantom: rho_cold = rho_ph/u inside r_sp raises the ENCLOSED mass, and DeltaSigma = Sigma(<R) - Sigma(R) then stays high outside r_sp (A = 1.6-1.7 at 1.7-2.5 Mpc against 0.93-1.06 measured). The 3D model is rejected at 5 sigma, so the measured step is a statement about the projected ratio u(R), i.e. about the phantom's radial SHAPE

  NFW cold sector, c = 4.5 (1 param): chi2 = 14.0/7 = 2.00, M_c = 1.02e+14 Msun
  NFW cold sector, c free  (2 param): chi2 = 5.1/6 = 0.85, M_c = 1.37e+14, c = 2.5
  NFW(c free) resid/sd = -0.4 -1.2 -0.2 -0.7 +0.9 +0.7 -2.3 +1.1
K20 PASS NFW(c=4.5) chi2/dof = 2.00; NFW(c free) 0.85 with M_c = 1.37e+14, c = 2.5 NFW(c free) chi2/dof < 1.5 (i.e. it also fits) :: HONEST LIMIT: a smooth NFW cold sector also fits the eight bins (chi2/dof = 0.85 with c free, 2.00 at c = 4.5) -- the profile alone does NOT single out the law+step. What the profile does establish is that the law's OWN phantom shape is wrong (u=1 excluded) and that the correction is not a constant (u=const excluded)

  transition width scan (projected step smoothed in log R; v profiled out at each width):
